<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Lesson Summary</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01603</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Lesson Summary</md:title>
    <md:uuid>ce1bbc76-8848-4e7d-9af1-fc75fb6cba26</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section id="sect-00001"><para id="para-00001">In this lesson, you learned how to:</para>
<list id="list-00001">
  <item>Multiply monomials.</item>
  <item>Multiply a polynomial by a monomial.</item>
  <item>Multiply binomials.</item>
  <item>Multiply a polynomial by a polynomial.</item>
  <item>Multiply special products.</item>
  <item>Multiply polynomial functions.</item>
</list>
<para id="para-00002">Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that helped you reach those goals:</para>
<list id="list-00002">
  <item>6.2.1: Multiplying Monomials
    <list id="list-00003">
    <item>In this activity, you learned how to multiply monomials by other monomials. You used properties of exponents when multiplying variables with different exponents.</item>
  </list></item>
  
  <item>6.2.2: Multiplying Binomials
    <list id="list-00004">
      <item>In this activity, you multiplied binomials using the Distributive Property, the FOIL method, and Vertical Alignment.</item>
      <item>6.2.2: Self Check</item>
      <item>6.2.2: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
 </item>
  <item>6.2.3: Multiplying a Polynomial by a Polynomial
    <list id="list-00005">
      <item>In this activity, you multiplied polynomials using the Distributive Property and Vertical Alignment.</item>
      <item>6.2.3: Self Check</item>
      <item>6.2.3: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
 </item>
  <item>6.2.4: Multiplying Special Products
    <list id="list-00006">
      <item>In this activity, you learned how to use patterns to quickly multiply binomial squares. You also learned how to multiply conjugate pairs using the Difference of Squares Pattern.</item>
      <item>6.2.4: Self Check</item>
      <item>6.2.4: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
 </item>
  <item>6.2.5: Multiplying Polynomial Functions
    <list id="list-00007">
    <item>In this activity, you continued to practice multiplying polynomials in polynomial function form.</item>
  </list></item>
  
</list>
<para id="para-00003">After these activities, you completed the following <emphasis>practice</emphasis>:</para>
<list id="list-00008">
  <item>6.2.6: Practice</item>
</list>
<section class="checking-in" id="sect-00002"><title>Checking In</title><exercise id="fd6140d0-680d-4452-8388-6b52ec716fbb" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00001"><para id="para-00004">On a scale of 1 to 5, how confident do you feel about the learning goals of this lesson?</para></problem><solution id="sol-00001"><para id="para-00005">Nice reflection! You learn more when you take the time to reflect on your thinking.</para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
</document>
